Nit: could you add a test with an old wait?

The `isOperationUpdatedSinceLastInvocation` check keeps an operation that finished in an *older* invocation in replay mode. `waitAsyncThenStep_intermediateStepStaysReplay` already covers this check through the `middle` step. Waits and callbacks run the same lines today, so they should behave the same way.

A test with an old wait would stop a later change from breaking this for waits only, for example if the mode switch moves into `WaitOperation`. It needs three invocations, so `w1` is old by the last one:

```java
var states = new ArrayList<String>();
var runner = LocalDurableTestRunner.create(String.class, (input, ctx) -> {
    ctx.wait("w1", Duration.ofSeconds(1));
    states.add("afterW1=" + ctx.isReplaying());
    ctx.wait("w2", Duration.ofSeconds(1));
    states.add("afterW2=" + ctx.isReplaying());
    return "done";
});

assertEquals(ExecutionStatus.PENDING, runner.run("x").getStatus());
runner.advanceTime();
assertEquals(ExecutionStatus.PENDING, runner.run("x").getStatus());
states.clear();
runner.advanceTime();
assertEquals(ExecutionStatus.SUCCEEDED, runner.run("x").getStatus());
assertEquals(List.of("afterW1=true", "afterW2=false"), states);
```

